tors trajectories, tool traces, rewards, and training statistics; diagnoses failures and uninformative interactions; and proposes targeted modifications to the user simulator, environment, reward design, and RL configuration. Validated changes are hot-swapped into the ongoing run, allowing the training setup to evolve together with the policy. These adaptations also persist across runs, so later training can build on previously discovered improvements rather than restarting from a fixed setup. We enable this process through an editable symbolic representation of user and environment dynamics, while the agent remains a neural LLM optimized with RL. Across three interactive-agent benchmarks and two backbone models, EAU consistently outperforms prior RL methods, improving the overall score over the strongest baseline by 14.7--15.0% and increasing successful task completion on ColBench by up to 36.7%, showing that co-evolving the training system with the policy can substantially improve multi-turn RL.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEAU：用于训练以用户为中心的智能体的环境-智能体-用户协同进化框架 | Arxiv - DeepPaper (https://arxiv.deeppaper.ai/papers/2610.16523v1)\nciteturn104search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 days ago; Crawled: 2 days ago; Image: arXiv 2610.16523v1\n\n# EAU：用于训练以用户为中心的智能体的环境-智能体-用户协同进化框架\n\n## EAU: Environment-Agent-User Co-evolution for Training User-Centric Agents\n\n### 主要贡献\n\n提出了一个元智能体框架（EAU），能够在训练过程中动态调整环境、用户模拟器和奖励设计，从而在多轮智能体任务中实现了显著的性能提升。\n\n### 摘要\n\n训练大语言模型（LLM）智能体与用户进行多轮交互具有挑战性，因为学习信号不仅取决于智能体，还取决于用户模拟器和环境，它们共同塑造了智能体的体验。模拟用户可能是随机或不一致的，而环境可能包含不可靠的工具、不完整的状态覆盖和错误的验证器。以往的研究主要通过奖励塑造或更密集的监督来解决由此产生的不稳定性，同时将这些组件视为固定的。我们引入了 EAU，这是一个用于环境-智能体-用户协同进化的元智能体框架。在训练过程中，EAU 监控轨迹、工具跟踪、奖励和训练统计数据；诊断故障和无信息的交互；并对用户模拟器、环境、奖励设计和强化学习配置提出针对性的修改。经过验证的更改会被热插拔到正在进行的运行中，使训练设置能够与策略一起进化。这些适应性在多次运行中持续存在，因此后续的训练可以建立在先前发现的改进之上，而不是从固定的设置重新开始。我们通过用户和环境动态的可编辑符号表示来实现这一过程，而智能体则保持为通过强化学习优化的神经 LLM。在三个交互式智能体基准测试和两个骨干模型上，EAU 始终优于先前的强化学习方法，将总分比最强的基线提高了 14.7%--15.0%，并将 ColBench 上的任务成功完成率提高了高达 36.7%，这表明使训练系统与策略协同进化可以显著改善多轮强化学习。\n\n### 总结\n\nEAU 是一个元智能体框架，通过环境、用户模拟器和智能体策略的协同进化，提升了多轮强化学习训练的稳定性和性能。\n\n### 研究领域\n\ncs.AI cs.CL cs.LG\n\n### arXiv\n\nImage: arXiv 2610.16523v1\n\n### 论文类型\n\nframework Method\n\n### 领域应用\n\nReinforcement Learning LLM Agent\n\n作者\n\nMin Cai, Dan Zhang, Gao Xing, Libin Ma, Zhaohui Xu, Xi Ye\n\n提交日期\n\n2026年10月12日--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\narXiv Troller (https://arxiv-troller.com/?q=paper%3A+2605.02624)\nciteturn104search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; arXiv:2610.16523\nEAU: Environment-Agent-User Co-evolution for Training User-Centric Agents\n\nMin Cai, Dan Zhang, Gao Xing et al.\n\narXiv:2610.16523\n\nAuthors: Min Cai, Dan Zhang, Gao Xing, Libin Ma, Zhaohui Xu, Xi Ye\n\nSubmitted: Oct 2026 | Updated: Oct 2026\n\nTraining LLM agents to interact with users over multiple turns is challenging because the learning signal depends not only on the agent, but also on the user simulator and environment, which jointly shape the agent's experience. Simulated users can be stochastic or inconsistent, while environments may contain unreliable tools, incomplete state coverage, and incorrect verifiers. Prior work mainly addresses the resulting instability through reward shaping or denser supervision, while treating these components as fixed. We instead introduce EAU, a meta-agent framework for environment--agent--user co-evolution. During training, EAU monitors trajectories, tool traces, rewards, and training statistics; diagnoses failures and uninformative interactions; and proposes targeted modifications to the user simulator, environment, reward design, and RL configuration. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSearch & Read arXiv Research Papers | ArcXiv (https://arcxiv.org/)\nciteturn104search9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; # Search and read arXiv research papers. ... Search millions of papers by title, au